<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5916" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzācĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βυσσᾶτις</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a province in</i> Africa Propria, <i>between the river Triton and the Lesser Syrtis</i>, <i><span class="en">Varr.
				R. R. 1, 44, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 5, 4, 3, § 24</span></i>; <i><span class="en">17, 5, 3, §
			41</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzācēnus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of Byzacium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">provincia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 1, 27, 2</span></i>
			; Cod. Th. 1, 27, 2.—As <i>subst.</i>:
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzācēni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Byzacium</i>, Cod. Th. 11, 1,
			29.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bȳzācĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sil.
					9, 204</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
